<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  GrimTerraTexPaths_Fix.xml                 Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-20
  ============================================================================

  GRiNDTerra Biomes (GRimTerra.Biomesmod, workshop 3537211820) ships three
  texPaths pointing at folders that do not exist. THE ART IS ALL PRESENT -
  only the paths are wrong, and all three are in the SECOND lifeStages entry,
  i.e. the JUVENILE stage. Baby and adult render correctly, which is why this
  went unnoticed.

  Verified against the mod's own Textures tree, 2026-08-20:
    Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimTortoise/   holds GRimTortoiseA_*.png
                                       and Dessicated_GRimTortoiseA_*.png
    Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimPinkbird/   holds GRimPinkbird_*.png

    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/TortoiseGRim/GRimTortoiseA        words transposed
    want  Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimTortoise/GRimTortoiseA

    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/Tortoise/Dessicated_GRimTortoiseA
    want  Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimTortoise/Dessicated_GRimTortoiseA
          ⚠️ that one points at VANILLA's Tortoise folder. It logs nothing until
          a dessicated corpse exists, so it never appears in a load harvest.

    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimPinkBird/GRimPinkbird          capital B
    want  Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimPinkbird/GRimPinkbird

  🔑 THE CAPITAL-B ONE IS THE INSTRUCTIVE CASE. Windows' filesystem is
  case-insensitive but RimWorld's content index is NOT, so that path resolves
  perfectly from a shell and still fails in game. Never settle a texPath
  question with `ls`.

  🪤 THEY ARE ON PawnKindDef, NOT ThingDef. The animal's ThingDef carries
  race/lifeStages; these three sit on the PAWNKIND's own lifeStages, which is a
  different node on a different def with the same-looking shape. An xpath aimed
  at ThingDef matches nothing here - and a PatchOperation that matches nothing
  logs nothing, so it would have looked exactly like a fix.

  Each operation targets the node BY ITS CURRENT VALUE rather than by position.
  li[2] would be correct today and wrong the moment anything inserts a life
  stage, and a value predicate cannot drift: only the broken node carries the
  broken string, so the op either hits the thing it names or hits nothing.

  🪤 THE PREDICATE GOES ON THE PARENT, NOT ON THE texPath ITSELF. The obvious
  form, texPath[.="..."], is XPath 1.0 and RimWorld would accept it - but the
  offline validator walks the defs with ElementTree, which does not implement a
  self-predicate and reports 0 matches. The form below,
  bodyGraphicData[texPath="..."]/texPath, is a CHILD-VALUE predicate and is the
  house form both engines agree on, the same shape as li[kindDef="Combat"].

  ⛔ DO NOT EDIT THE WORKSHOP FOLDER. Steam overwrites it on the next update.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>GRiNDTerra Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="GRimTortoise"]/lifeStages/li/bodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/TortoiseGRim/GRimTortoiseA"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimTortoise/GRimTortoiseA</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="GRimTortoise"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/Tortoise/Dessicated_GRimTortoiseA"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimTortoise/Dessicated_GRimTortoiseA</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="GRimPinkbird"]/lifeStages/li/bodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimPinkBird/GRimPinkbird"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/GRimPinkbird/GRimPinkbird</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
